{"name":"Stairway to Heaven","hex":"#67716e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stairway","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of steps, with or without a case, that allow one to walk up or down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stairway"},{"term":"heaven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sky, specifically:\n The distant sky in which the sun, moon, and stars appear or move; the firmament; the celestial spheres.\n\n The near sky in which weather, flying animals, etc. appear;  the atmosphere; the climate.\n\n A model displaying the movement of the celestial bodies, an orrery.","The distant sky in which the sun, moon, and stars appear or move; the firmament; the celestial spheres."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To transport to the abode of God, the gods, or the blessed.","To beatify, enchant, or please greatly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heaven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stairway to Heaven","blocks":[{"text":"\"Stairway to Heaven\" is a song by the English rock band Led Zeppelin, released on 8 November 1971 on the band's untitled fourth studio album, by Atlantic Records. Composed by the band's guitarist Jimmy Page with lyrics written by lead singer Robert Plant, it is widely regarded as one of the greatest rock songs of all time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Stairway_to_Heaven_by_Led_Zeppelin_US_promotional_single.png/330px-Stairway_to_Heaven_by_Led_Zeppelin_US_promotional_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stairway_to_Heaven"},{"title":"Stairway to Heaven (South Korean TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Stairway to Heaven is a 2003 South Korean television series starring Choi Ji-woo, Kwon Sang-woo, Shin Hyun-joon, and Kim Tae-hee. It aired on SBS from 3 December 2003 to 5 February 2004 on Wednesdays and Thursdays at 21:55 for 20 episodes. The title of the show comes from the Led Zeppelin song of the same name, which is frequently used in the soundtrack."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/63/Stairway_to_Heaven-poster.jpg/330px-Stairway_to_Heaven-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stairway_to_Heaven_(South_Korean_TV_series)"},{"title":"Staircase","blocks":[{"text":"A staircase or stairway is a flight or series of flights of stairs. It is used to connect walkways between floors so that one can move in height. A stairwell is a shaft in a building where a staircase is located. In buildings with several housing units, a stairway can be a necessary common area for getting to and from apartments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Skylight%2C_chandelier_and_stairs%2C_Ashmolean_Museum%2C_Oxford.jpg/330px-Skylight%2C_chandelier_and_stairs%2C_Ashmolean_Museum%2C_Oxford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staircase"},{"title":"Heaven","blocks":[{"text":"Heaven, or the Heavens, is a common religious cosmological or supernatural place where beings such as deities, angels, souls, saints, or venerated ancestors are said to originate, be enthroned, or reside. According to the beliefs of some religions, heavenly beings can descend to Earth or incarnate and earthly beings can ascend to Heaven in the afterlife or, in exceptional cases, enter Heaven without dying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Paradiso_Canto_31_%28148200393%29.jpg/330px-Paradiso_Canto_31_%28148200393%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heaven"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/%D0%94%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BC%D0%B8_%D0%9F%D1%8D%D0%B9%D0%B4%D0%B6.jpg/500px-%D0%94%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BC%D0%B8_%D0%9F%D1%8D%D0%B9%D0%B4%D0%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/%D0%94%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BC%D0%B8_%D0%9F%D1%8D%D0%B9%D0%B4%D0%B6.jpg/500px-%D0%94%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BC%D0%B8_%D0%9F%D1%8D%D0%B9%D0%B4%D0%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jimmy Page used a double-necked guitar to perform \"Stairway to Heaven\" live.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D0%94%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BC%D0%B8_%D0%9F%D1%8D%D0%B9%D0%B4%D0%B6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/VaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg/500px-VaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/VaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg/1280px-VaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/VaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg/500px-VaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spiral staircase (double helix) in the Vatican Museums","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVaticanMuseumStaircase.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Riga_Jugendstiltreppe.jpg/500px-Riga_Jugendstiltreppe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Riga_Jugendstiltreppe.jpg/1280px-Riga_Jugendstiltreppe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Riga_Jugendstiltreppe.jpg/500px-Riga_Jugendstiltreppe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spiral staircase in Riga (Art Nouveau)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARiga_Jugend